CRE oracle capital-flow snapshots
├── when a snapshot precedes or follows a withdrawal
│   ├── the 1000 minus 150 example yields 850 in both cases
│   ├── withdrawing everything leaves zero rather than restoring stale assets
│   └── allocations and withdrawals after a snapshot are applied exactly once
├── when reading the accepted latestSnapshot tuple
│   ├── oracle NAV and block remain unchanged across later allocations and withdrawals
│   └── adapter live NAV follows flows and flow-neutral reports pass zero deviation limits
├── when checking movement limits
│   ├── compare NAV with the historical flow-adjusted baseline
│   └── requests and post-snapshot withdrawals do not become investment gains or losses
├── when reconciling signed accounting
│   ├── realized profits allow cumulative net capital to become negative
│   ├── negative historical baseline and overflow reject normal delivery but are bypassed by exact guard review
│   ├── negative current NAV still rejects delivery and guard review
│   ├── signed overflow, negative reconciliation and out-of-range reports revert without replacing a cached deviation
│   ├── intermediate subtraction still reverts if later flow addition would cancel it
│   └── invalid current NAV takes precedence over deviation and preserves accepted state and liquidity reserves
└── when authenticating a rejected snapshot
    ├── preserve the exact four-word payload for review
    ├── keep accepted NAV usable through the production withdrawal path
    └── applying the reviewed snapshot includes all intervening capital flows
